click: x=-2.750 y=0.925 z=0.750
click: x=-2.150 y=0.925 z=0.375

[ceiling] This is the 6.70 by 7.15 mm print-down roof of the open +Y T-slot, underside Z 2.40 with 1.80 mm of solid stock above it. The keeper is supports-off and its two lips begin directly on the bed. Native readings of the identical N08K/N12K/N24K slot roofs in kit-01 begin at nozzle Z 2.60 with 17 Bridge and 2 Overhang-wall deposits apiece, no slot support, then solid infill at Z 2.84; the 0.24 mm model step gives nominal first underside Z 2.36 rather than CAD Z 2.40. The CAD 0.30 mm air above the matched T-head is retained. Printed roof sag and sliding force are unmeasured.
alternatives: A 3.00 mm roof adds 1.20 mm above the keeper without changing its slot, but enlarges the keeper and its clearance envelope. A sloped roof changes the flat roof-air convention. A separately printed bed-facing cap avoids this bridge but introduces another joint and alignment tolerance.
file: hardware/printed-parts/calibration/soda-studies/parts/ns20k-neck-t-slot-keeper.step
